          "secNumber": "1.5",
          "heading": "Example: ranking candidate materials",
          "content": "Suppose a prediction service assigns a high stiffness-to-density ratio to two alloys. Before procurement, define the component's geometry freedom, load spectrum, minimum fracture toughness, joining method, environmental exposure, inspection intervals and intended life. Ask whether the training data contain the new chemistry family and manufacturing condition. Independently verify unit conversions and the candidate's actual composition; use higher-fidelity calculations for edge cases, then appropriate physical testing. Estimate total accepted-part cost rather than raw feedstock cost, including yields and replacement frequency. A rational result may be to collect more measurements or reject both materials even if one is the numerical winner.",
